* parameter file for HyRes amino acid adducts and modified residues
* (e.g. fluorescent dyes attached to Cys); companion of top_adducts.inp.
* Load together with param_hyres_mix.inp and param_metabolome.inp; utils.load_ff('Adduct').
* Dye linker bonded terms fitted from the AA A488-Cys trajectory (FRET/A488/amber);
* bonds inside the rigid amide + phenyl + xanthene are K = 0 placeholders (use rigid bodies starting at the
* amide bead: A48/A59 A05, R48 A03, R59 A07, C3B A05; C66 imidazolium A06-A08 + A11-A24); amide-phenyl terms (M03-XAR, M03-XAR-XAR) then act inside the body.
*

BOND
!
!V(bond) = Kb(b - b0)**2
!
!Kb: kcal/mole/A**2
!b0: A
!
!atom type    Kb      b0
!## A48/A59 dye linker, Boltzmann inversion (moment matched, 300 K) of the AA A488-Cys
!## trajectory (FRET/A488/amber, 26110 frames; bonddist.xvg, A04-A05/A05-A06 from cg.xtc)
P1C   M07      9.81    2.777  ! CB-A01
M07   M07    495.82    2.899  ! A01-A02 (succinimide)
C3E   M07    258.97    2.300  ! A01-A03 and A02-A03 (shared); overrides param_metabolome C3E-M07
A2V   C3E      8.78    2.959  ! A03-A04; overrides param_metabolome C3E-A2V
A2V   M03      2.78    3.628  ! A04-A05; overrides param_metabolome M03-A2V
M03   XAR    267.79    2.700  ! A05-A06; inside the rigid body (amide + phenyl + xanthene)
!## bonds inside the rigid amide + phenyl + xanthene body: placeholders, K = 0
XAR   XAR      0.00    1.000  ! A48/A59/R48/R59 ring bonds
XAN   XAR      0.00    1.000
QAD   XAR      0.00    1.000  ! A07-A09 carboxylate
QDK   XAR      0.00    1.000  ! amine (A48/R48) and N(+) (A59/R59) beads
MSO   QDK      0.00    1.000  ! A48/R48
MSO   XAR      0.00    1.000  ! A59/R59
A2V   XAR      0.00    1.000  ! A59/R59
!## R59/R48 (dyes on RNA ends) junction terms, Boltzmann inversion (300 K) of the CG-mapped
!## rA19 HCG ensemble (FRET/rA19, 10000 models); same fitting as the A48/A59 linker
!## R48 terms refitted from the ensemble reweighted (max. entropy) to the experimental <E> = 0.55
!## (Nuesch et al., Nat Commun 2024); R59 terms from the unweighted ensemble
A2V   RP      12.22    3.577  ! R59 A01-+P
A2V   A5M      2.31    4.479  ! R59 A01-A02
A5M   M07      2.70    3.432  ! R59 A02-A03
RS1   M05      1.61    3.608  ! R48 -C1-A01
M05   P1T      8.43    2.902  ! R48 A01-A02
P1T   M03      2.95    3.444  ! R48 A02-A03; overrides param_metabolome P1T-M03
!## C3B (Cy3B) / C66 (CF660R) on Cys, C2R linker. Both dyes carry the same C2R types (A04 = M3L), so C3B CB..A04 use the
!## C66 C2R terms below (succinimide CB-A01 ... A02-A03 as A48). The C3B junction to the core (A05, type XAR) and the C66 linker and propyl-sulfonate (A09/A10) by
!## Boltzmann inversion (moment matched, 300 K) of the CG-mapped all-atom MD of Ivanovic, Schuler & Best (Zenodo 13381447:
!## 16 IDPs labelled with Cy3B/CF660R, 3 x 2 us each, Amber ff99SBws; 480k frames pooled); C66 CB-A01 ... A02-A03
!## (succinimide) as A48. FRET/dye_mapping/zenodo/zenodo_fit.py
M3L   XAR     16.46    3.101  ! C3B A04-A05   (AA 3.11 +- 0.13)
C3E   M3L      3.16    2.972  ! C66/C3B A03-A04   (AA 3.04 +- 0.30)
M3L   A5L      3.31    3.545  ! C66 A04-A05   (AA 3.60 +- 0.30)
A5L   QdK      5.54    3.578  ! C66 A05-A06   (AA 3.61 +- 0.23)
QdK   A3S      6.78    2.853  ! C66 A08-A09   (AA 2.88 +- 0.21) propyl-sulfonate, flexible
A3S   MSO     46.76    3.049  ! C66 A09-A10   (AA 3.05 +- 0.08)
!## C3B/C66 rigid cores (C3B A05-A19, C66 A06-A08 + A11-A24; in the AA MD the C66 imidazolium rocks on the xanthene,
!## up to 1.0 A sd at A06 = N1 + CH2, frozen here): placeholders, K = 0
QDK   XAN      0.00    1.000  ! C3B indolenine N - polymethine centre
QDK   QDK      0.00    1.000  ! C66 imidazolium N - N

THETAS
!
!V(angle) = Ktheta(Theta - Theta0)**2
!
!Ktheta: kcal/mole/rad**2
!Theta0: degrees
!
!atom types     Ktheta    Theta0
!## A48/A59 dye linker; ReB angles (V = K (t-t0)^2/sin^2 t), K and t0 chosen so the 300 K
!## distribution reproduces the AA mean and standard deviation (angle_0-4.xvg)
P1C   M07   M07     17.23     92.1  ! CB-A01-A02     (AA  91.9 +-  7.1)
M07   C3E   A2V      4.07    128.7  ! A02-A03-A04    (AA 122.3 +- 12.3)
C3E   A2V   M03      1.27    162.2  ! A03-A04-A05    (AA 138.0 +- 19.9)
A2V   M03   XAR      3.19    129.1  ! A04-A05-A06    (AA 121.4 +- 13.6)
M03   XAR   XAR      9.97    172.2  ! A05-A06-A08    (AA 170.9 +-  2.2); inside the rigid body: near-linear, unstable at 8 fs if flexible
!## R59/R48 (dyes on RNA ends) junction terms; ReB angles moment matched (300 K) to the CG-mapped
!## rA19 HCG ensemble (FRET/rA19, 10000 models); same fitting as the A48/A59 linker
!## R48 terms refitted from the ensemble reweighted (max. entropy) to the experimental <E> = 0.55
!## (Nuesch et al., Nat Commun 2024); R59 terms from the unweighted ensemble
A2V   RP    RS1      3.85    104.5  ! R59 A01-+P-+C1   (AA 101.8 +- 13.2)
A5M   A2V   RP       0.94    150.4  ! R59 A02-A01-+P   (AA 126.4 +- 21.3)
A2V   A5M   M07      1.45    163.7  ! R59 A01-A02-A03   (AA 141.1 +- 19.1)
A5M   M07   M07      3.35    104.2  ! R59 A02-A03-A04   (AA 101.3 +- 13.9)
RP    RS1   M05      1.68    130.5  ! R48 -P--C1-A01   (AA 118.5 +- 17.4)
RS2   RS1   M05      2.50    100.6  ! R48 -C2--C1-A01   (AA  98.0 +- 15.4)
RS1   M05   P1T      2.77    110.4  ! R48 -C1-A01-A02   (AA 105.7 +- 14.8)
M05   P1T   M03      2.75    122.8  ! R48 A01-A02-A03   (AA 115.4 +- 14.6)
P1T   M03   XAR      1.55    134.3  ! R48 A02-A03-A04   (AA 120.6 +- 17.9)
!## C66 (CF660R) linker and propyl-sulfonate, C3B junction to the core; ReB angles moment matched (300 K) to the
!## CG-mapped all-atom MD (Zenodo 13381447; C3B A02-A03-A04 is the C66 term; CB-A01-A02 as A48)
C3E   M3L   XAR      1.77    141.5  ! C3B A03-A04-A05   (AA 127.1 +- 17.0)
M3L   XAR   XAR      4.49    116.0  ! C3B A04-A05-A06   (AA 111.8 +- 12.2)
M07   C3E   M3L      1.80    118.9  ! C66/C3B A02-A03-A04   (AA 110.4 +- 17.1)
C3E   M3L   A5L      1.20    150.1  ! C66 A03-A04-A05   (AA 129.2 +- 19.7)
M3L   A5L   QdK      1.35    160.4  ! C66 A04-A05-A06   (AA 137.8 +- 19.4)
A5L   QdK   A4H      3.90    129.8  ! C66 A05-A06-A07   (AA 123.1 +- 12.5)
A4H   QdK   A3S     23.59    105.1  ! C66 A07-A08-A09   (AA 104.4 +-  6.0)
QdK   A3S   MSO      5.75    148.9  ! C66 A08-A09-A10   (AA 143.1 +-  8.9)

PHI
!
!V(dihedral) = Kchi(1 + cos(n(chi) - delta))
!
!Kchi: kcal/mole
!n: multiplicity
!delta: degrees
!
!atom types             Kchi    n   delta
!## A48/A59 dye linker; fewest-term fit to dihed_0-4.xvg (300 K): one term (best n of 1-3) first, a second
!## only if it raises the overlap with the AA distribution by >= 0.03; parameters by minimum KL divergence
!## (overlap: 0.96, 0.81, 0.90, 0.89, 0.93)
P1C   M07   M07   C3E    15.548   1   -31.8  ! CB-A01-A02-A03 (succinimide ring, narrow: AA sd ~11 deg)
M07   M07   C3E   A2V     0.909   1     7.7  ! A01-A02-A03-A04
M07   M07   C3E   A2V     1.160   3   184.4
M07   C3E   A2V   M03     0.127   1  -202.7  ! A01-A03-A04-A05
C3E   A2V   M03   XAR     0.204   2  -187.5  ! A03-A04-A05-A06
A2V   M03   XAR   XAR     1.181   1     0.6  ! A04-A05-A06-A08
M03   XAR   XAR   XAR    11.916   1   177.3  ! A05-A06-A08-A07; inside the rigid body (ill-defined across the ~171 deg angle)
M03   XAR   XAR   XAR     3.023   2   -10.0
M03   XAR   XAR   XAR     0.231   3   132.8
!## R59/R48 (dyes on RNA ends) junction terms; fewest-term fit (300 K) to the CG-mapped rA19 HCG ensemble
!## (FRET/rA19, 10000 models), same rule as the A48/A59 linker: one term first, another only if the overlap
!## is < 0.85 and the extra term raises it by >= 0.03; parameters by minimum KL divergence
!## R48 terms from the ensemble reweighted (max. entropy) to the experimental <E> = 0.55
!## (Nuesch et al., Nat Commun 2024); R59 terms from the unweighted ensemble
A2V   RP    RS1   RS2     1.226  1   -173.5  ! R59 A01-+P-+C1-+C2 (overlap 0.93)
A2V   RP    RS1   RS2     0.474  3    -48.4
A5M   A2V   RP    RS1     0.550  1    203.9  ! R59 A02-A01-+P-+C1 (overlap 0.89)
A5M   A2V   RP    RS1     0.437  2   -222.2
A2V   A5M   M07   M07     0.568  1    -15.8  ! R59 A01-A02-A03-A04 (overlap 0.92)
A5M   M07   M07   C3E     7.482  1    -27.3  ! R59 A02-A03-A04-A05 (overlap 0.90)
RP    RS1   M05   P1T     0.909  1      8.8  ! R48 -P--C1-A01-A02 (overlap 0.94)
RP    RS1   M05   P1T     0.508  2     22.3
RS1   M05   P1T   M03     1.455  1   -178.1  ! R48 -C1-A01-A02-A03 (overlap 0.85; one term kept on purpose, two give 0.89)
M05   P1T   M03   XAR     2.651  1   -126.7  ! R48 A01-A02-A03-A04: one term for the main peak only (AA -60..150 deg, 79%,
!                                             mean 52 +- 30 deg); the minor peak near +-180 deg is dropped (overlap 0.73)
P1T   M03   XAR   XAR     0.894  1     23.8  ! R48 A02-A03-A04-A06 (overlap 0.94)
!## C66 (CF660R) linker and propyl-sulfonate, C3B junction to the core; one term per dihedral (best n of 1-3, minimum KL,
!## 300 K) fitted to the CG-mapped all-atom MD (Zenodo 13381447; C3B A01-A02-A03-A04 is the C66 term; CB-A01-A02-A03 as A48)
M07   C3E   M3L   XAR     0.428  1    170.5  ! C3B A01-A03-A04-A05 (overlap 0.75)
C3E   M3L   XAR   XAR     0.130  1    174.5  ! C3B A03-A04-A05-A06 (overlap 0.94)
M3L   XAR   XAR   XAR     1.103  1     -4.0  ! C3B A04-A05-A06-A07 (overlap 0.43: AA is bimodal at +-135 deg, one term cannot fit it)
M07   M07   C3E   M3L     1.011  2      0.6  ! C66/C3B A01-A02-A03-A04 (overlap 0.66)
M07   C3E   M3L   A5L     0.185  1   -174.0  ! C66 A01-A03-A04-A05 (overlap 0.91)
C3E   M3L   A5L   QdK     0.105  1   -161.3  ! C66 A03-A04-A05-A06 (overlap 0.97)
QdK   A4H   QdK   A5L     0.945  1     -1.5  ! C66 A08-A07-A06-A05 (overlap 0.67)
QdK   A4H   QdK   A3S     3.567  1     -0.7  ! C66 A06-A07-A08-A09 (overlap 0.67)
A4H   QdK   A3S   MSO     0.937  2      1.4  ! C66 A07-A08-A09-A10 (overlap 0.69)

IMPHI
!
!V(improper) = Kpsi(psi - psi0)**2
!
!Kpsi: kcal/mole/rad**2
!psi0: degrees
!
!atom types           Kpsi                   psi0

NONBONDED  NBXMOD 5  ATOM CDIEL SWITCH VATOM VDISTANCE VSWITCH -
     CUTNB 12.0  CTOFNB 12.0  CTONNB 11.0

!
!V(Lennard-Jones) = Eps,i,j[(Rmin,i,j/ri,j)**12 - 2(Rmin,i,j/ri,j)**6]
!
!epsilon: kcal/mole, Eps,i,j = sqrt(eps,i * eps,j)
!Rmin/2: A, Rmin,i,j = Rmin/2,i + Rmin/2,j
!
!atom  ignored    epsilon      Rmin/2   ignored   eps,1-4       Rmin/2,1-4
!
!## dye beads
XAN      0.00     -0.1500      2.3444   0.00     -0.1500       2.3444 ! dye xanthene C9;
XAR      0.00     -0.1500      2.3444   0.00     -0.1500       2.3444 ! dye aromatic ring bead
!## C66 (CF660R) types, nonbonded copied from the analogue in brackets. A5L/A3S are separate names only so that
!## their fitted bonded terms do not clash with A2V-QdK of param_metabolome; nonbonded they are A2V (rows below).
M3L      0.00     -0.0720      2.2759   0.00     -0.0720       2.2759 ! C2R linker CH2-NH-C(=O) (M03)
A5L      0.00     -0.2001      2.7541   0.00     -0.2001       2.7541 ! butyl -(CH2)4- (A2V)
A3S      0.00     -0.2001      2.7541   0.00     -0.2001       2.7541 ! propyl on the imidazolium (A2V)

NBFIX
!                 Emin         Rmin
!                 (kcal/mol)   (A)
!# dye xanthene centre (XAN, A488 and A594) - aromatic stacking, set like the cation-pi rows of
!# param_hyres_mix.inp: Emin = 0.148 * PMF well depth, Rmin = sum of Rmin/2.
!# Trp: experimental dye-Trp Kd (A488 59 mM, A594 33 mM; Best et al., Biophys J 2015, Table 1)
!# -> dG0 -1.7/-2.0 kcal/mol -> well depth ~ -2.5/-2.9 (bound volume 0.3-0.5 nm^3) -> Emin ~ -0.40.
!# Tyr/Phe: no data; scaled from Trp by the Arg preferences (QdR-A2W -0.70, -P1Y -0.65, -A1F -0.50).
XAN       A2W      -0.4000      4.4314
XAN       P1Y      -0.3700      4.7968
XAN       A1F      -0.2900      4.9858
!# Arg: xanthene-guanidinium stacking, between the HyRes Arg-Phe (-0.50) and Arg-Trp (-0.70) cation-pi
!# rows (xanthene >= indole in size, but its delocalised + charge weakens cation-pi); no XAN-QdK row,
!# since QdK is also the dye's own amine/N(+) bead type.
XAN       QdR      -0.6000      4.8807
!# RNA bases (iConRNA): xanthene-base stacking on base bead 1, as the aromatic-base rows of param_RNA_mix.inp
!# (Rmin 4.5). G: xanthene-dGMP ~ 0.85-0.9 x xanthene-Trp association (TMR-dGMP 52 M^-1 vs rhodamine-Trp
!# 61 M^-1) -> 0.9 x XAN-A2W; A/C from the iCon Trp-base pattern (A2W-RA1/RG1/RC1 -0.86/-0.96/-0.65);
!# U set weaker than that pattern (-0.33) by choice.
XAN       RA1      -0.3300      4.5000
XAN       RG1      -0.3700      4.5000
XAN       RC1      -0.2500      4.5000
XAN       RU1      -0.2000      4.5000


END
